  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Electric field inside the uniformly charged sphere varies linearly, $E=\\frac{k Q}{R^{3}} r,(r \\leq R)$ while outside the sphere, it varies as inverse\nsquare of distance, $E=\\frac{k Q}{r^{2}} ;(r \\geq R)$ which is correctly represented in option (c).",
    "image": null
